INSERT INTO public.content_schedule (title, channel_label, scheduled_date, status, brand, body, cta, post_type, notes) SELECT 'The five documents that decide your claim.', 'Email', '2026-08-24', 'drafted', 'EvidLY', 'A fire is survivable. A denied claim is harder.

When a carrier reviews a commercial kitchen loss, the difference between paid and denied usually comes down to five things: your hood cleaning records, your suppression service history, your inspection history, your employee training logs, and photographic evidence of condition.

Most kitchens have some of it. Almost none have all five — organized, dated, and retrievable in the moment someone asks.

That last part is what gets people. The records exist somewhere. They''re in a vendor''s truck, an email thread from two years ago, a binder in an office that may also have burned, and someone''s phone. Existing somewhere and being producible in ten minutes are not the same thing, and only one of them helps.

EvidLY keeps the proof where you can produce it.

I''ve watched a fully covered loss become a denied claim because the paperwork didn''t exist in retrievable form. The fire was survivable. The denial wasn''t. That was a family''s livelihood, gone on documentation.

Predict the lapse. Reduce the cost.

Arthur Haggerty
Founder, EvidLY
