INSERT INTO public.content_schedule (title, channel_label, scheduled_date, status, brand, body, cta, post_type, notes) SELECT 'The public record is proof of something. Just be clear what.', 'Email', '2026-09-09', 'drafted', 'ScoreTable', 'A published inspection result proves that a specific authority evaluated a specific kitchen on a specific day against a specific set of categories.

That''s a real, verifiable fact. It''s worth having and it''s the reason ScoreTable exists.

What it doesn''t prove is broader than people assume. It doesn''t prove conditions today. It doesn''t prove anything about fire safety, which is a separate authority in every county we cover. It doesn''t prove that categories the county chose not to evaluate are in good order.

We''re specific about this because the alternative — presenting county data as a general safety verdict — would perform better and would be a claim the data can''t support.

Every ScoreTable county page shows what the county evaluates, how its methodology works, the date of the record, and where the official source lives. If a county publishes nothing, the page says so. We don''t estimate.

Proof of something specific beats a confident claim about something general.

The Score Behind Every Table.

